.TH RUMB 1 2026-10-21 rumb "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rumb, rumb\-scan \- track software health and spot trouble early
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rumb
.RB [ \-\-demo ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-anim ]
.RB [ \-\-theme
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-since
.IR time ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-aur ]
.br
.B rumb
.BR \-\-themes " | " \-\-version " | " \-\-help
.br
.B rumb\-scan
.RB [ \-\-json " | " \-\-stream ]
.RB [ \-\-since
.IR time ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-aur ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rumb
is a terminal dashboard for Arch Linux and Omarchy.
It shows what the next update brings and what is already failing:
pending repository and AUR updates ranked by risk,
and the crashes, failed units, journal errors and Hyprland config errors
since the last completed full system upgrade,
each tied to the package that owns it,
together with the Arch news published since then.
On Omarchy, a pending Omarchy update also shows what its release notes fix.
.PP
rumb only reads.
It never runs
.B sudo
or asks for root.
Pending repository updates come from
.BR checkupdates (8),
which syncs a temporary copy of the package databases
and never touches the system's own.
.PP
In the middle an eye reads the scan.
Its pupil types each command that
.B rumb\-scan
runs and the answer it gets,
the raw data runs through the white of the eye,
and signals carry each result to its tile.
The eye looks at the tile it is reading.
.PP
After the scan rumb keeps following the pacman log and the journal,
and checks again when a package transaction completes.
.PP
The dashboard needs a terminal of at least 150x44.
A smaller terminal shows the size it needs until the window is large enough.
When output is not a terminal or
.B NO_COLOR
is set,
rumb prints the plain text report of
.B rumb\-scan
instead.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Play bundled demo data instead of checking this system.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-anim
Show the results without animation.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colors to use.
By default rumb uses the current Omarchy theme and follows it when it changes;
without Omarchy it uses labra.
.B omarchy
selects the current Omarchy theme explicitly.
.TP
.B \-\-themes
List the theme names.
.TP
.BI \-\-since " time"
Look for problems since
.IR time ,
for example
.RB \(dq "7 days ago" \(dq.
The default is the last completed full system upgrade.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-aur
Skip the AUR update check.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B 1\(en5
Show or hide the instruments, the subsystems with the eye, the updates, the problems and the live events.
When the updates panel is large enough, 3 switches it between the map, the rows and hidden.
The map shows every pending update by risk and subsystem,
with the dependencies of the selected update.
.TP
.B tab
Move the focus between the instruments, the subsystems and the lists.
.TP
.BR left ", " right
Move the focus between the lists, or between the instruments or the parts of the subsystems when they have it.
.TP
.BR up ", " down ", " PgUp ", " PgDn ", " Home ", " End
Select a row.
Up on the first row moves the focus to the subsystems, or to the instruments when the subsystems are hidden;
from the subsystems up moves it to the instruments and down back to the lists.
.TP
.B enter
Open the selected row, instrument or part.
.TP
.BR / ", " f
Filter the focused list.
.TP
.B j
Show the journal of the selected problem.
.TP
.B e
Export a Markdown report to
.IR ~/rumb\-exports .
.TP
.B esc
Close, clear or leave the instruments or the subsystems.
.TP
.B r
Scan again.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH RUMB\-SCAN
.B rumb\-scan
runs the checks that rumb shows and prints them as a text report.
rumb starts it on its own; it can also be run directly, for example from a script.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the forecast as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-stream
Print one JSON event per line while the checks run,
then keep following the package manager log and the journal.
.PP
.BR \-\-since " and " \-\-no\-aur
work as for rumb.
AUR updates are checked with
.B yay
or
.B paru
when one of them is installed,
and reported as not checked otherwise.
The Arch news needs
.BR xmllint .
The Omarchy release notes are read from the GitHub API,
only when an Omarchy update is pending.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUMB_THEME
Theme to use when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B RUMB_SCAN
Path of the
.B rumb\-scan
to run.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set and not empty, print the plain text report.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/omarchy/current/theme/colors.toml
The current Omarchy theme
.RI ( ~/.config/omarchy/current/theme/colors.toml
on older Omarchy).
.TP
.I /var/log/pacman.log
The package manager log, or the
.B LogFile
that
.BR pacman.conf (5)
names.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR checkupdates (8),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR coredumpctl (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
